;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (Reducible: nth traps out of range), §1.2 P5 (what Clojure throws on, traps here)
;; expect: trap
;; trap:   nth: index out of range
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: range-by
;; (range-by 0 10 3) is 0 3 6 9: four elements, so index 4 is one past the last. nth of an integer range is a
;; closed form, which checks the index against the count and traps with the function's name, as the default
;; nth of every other source does (case 016).
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq))

(defun main () -> i64 (nth (range-by 0 10 3) 4))
